      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَبْرَيْتُهَا</span></b> , (S, M, K,) i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">النَّاقَةَ</span>, (S, M,) <i>I put
a</i> [<i>ring such as is termed</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرَة</span> <i>in her</i> (a camel's)
<i>nose;</i> (S, M, K;) as also ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بَرَوْتُهَا</span></b> : (IJ, M, K:)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابريتهُ</span>, namely, a camel, <i>I put him a</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بُرَة</span>.
(Msb.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ابرى</span> <i>Dust,</i> or <i>earth, came,</i> or <i>lighted,
upon it.</i> (K,* TA, in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">برى</span>.)

